00:25:34.020 --> 00:25:36.600
By the time Joe Sr. was recalled from London,

00:25:37.320 --> 00:25:39.320
reporters on both sides of the Atlantic

00:25:39.320 --> 00:25:43.210
were calling him a Hitler apologist, a defeatist.

00:25:45.800 --> 00:25:47.560
Nothing to say until I've seen the president.

00:25:50.040 --> 00:25:53.540
Joe Kennedy returned in disgrace and in the minority,

00:25:53.540 --> 00:25:58.170
and at some point he decided he was going to make a speech

00:25:58.170 --> 00:25:59.330
defending his position.

00:26:00.350 --> 00:26:06.800
Joe had dozens of people he could have called on—journalists, newspapermen, historians,

00:26:07.080 --> 00:26:13.230
researchers. He had professional speechwriters working for him, but he asked Jack to do it.

00:26:14.410 --> 00:26:20.380
Jack Kennedy wasn't a puppet. He didn't swallow his father's beliefs. And he said to him,

00:26:20.500 --> 00:26:25.980
you can talk about the need for compromise and for negotiations,

00:26:25.980 --> 00:26:29.680
but say over and over and over again that you hate.

00:26:30.120 --> 00:26:38.890
nazism you hate fascism you hate hitler and don't use the word isolationist or appeaser joe

00:26:38.890 --> 00:26:46.980
eventually gave that speech and he followed some but not enough of his son's recommendations and

00:26:47.580 --> 00:26:55.700
ended up further on the outs with the roosevelt administration of course there's a risk in any

00:26:55.700 --> 00:26:59.970
course of action but all doubts as to what is the

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:10.220
The best thing we can do should be resolved in the one statement, how can we best keep out of war?

00:27:11.740 --> 00:27:21.150
Jack initially defended his father's isolationism, but as time went on, he realized that the United States needed to help Britain to get in the game, to fight for freedom.

00:27:21.330 --> 00:27:24.970
I mean, his father was dead set against American intervention. Jack becomes fort.

00:27:32.780 --> 00:27:35.940
Our cadet Joseph T. Kennedy Jr. reports for preliminary training.

00:27:36.350 --> 00:27:38.710
With other college men, he'll try for Navy wing.

00:27:39.560 --> 00:27:44.360
The older Kennedy boys were doing more than talking war in 1941.

00:27:46.070 --> 00:27:48.570
Joe Jr. signed on as a flyer for the Navy,

00:27:49.040 --> 00:27:51.480
even though the U.S. had not yet entered the fight.

00:27:55.770 --> 00:27:58.790
Jack was no less keen to get his shot at glory.

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:07.210
came, but he was unable to get past the military doctors. His poor health was impossible to miss.

