00:31:58.880 --> 00:31:59.180
August.

00:32:01.340 --> 00:32:05.660
Out on a routine mission, Kennedy had his vessel idling in open water.

00:32:07.000 --> 00:32:13.870
When a Japanese destroyer emerged out of the darkness, racing at 40 knots, and split his boat in half,

00:32:20.420 --> 00:32:22.620
two of his crewmen were killed immediately.

00:32:24.310 --> 00:32:29.980
It took Kennedy nearly three hours, swimming around in the dark, to gather the survivors onto...

00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:37.520
was left of his PT boat. His engineer, Pappy McMahon, was badly burned in excruciating pain

00:32:37.520 --> 00:32:46.080
and helpless. They were still stranded in open water at daybreak. Mid-afternoon, what was left

00:32:46.080 --> 00:32:54.270
of PT-109 was beginning to sink and it looked like they had been left for dead. They're drifting,

00:32:54.430 --> 00:32:59.510
holding on to the hull and drifting in the water when he sees a group of islands about three miles

00:32:59.510 --> 00:32:59.710
So

00:33:00.410 --> 00:33:02.890
